# General Performance (Telegram-level)

## Threading

- Network/disk I/O: always on `@IoDispatcher` (Dispatchers.IO)
- Room DAO calls: always `suspend` functions called from IO dispatcher or `appScope` (which uses IO)
- State updates: OK on any dispatcher (StateFlow is thread-safe)
- Compose: never block the main thread — no `runBlocking`, no synchronous network or disk
- Proto parsing (`parseFrom`): do on IO dispatcher, not main

## Memory

- NEVER hold references to Activity/Context in Singletons
- `evictChannel()` evicts in-memory cache only — data stays in Room DB for next cold start
- Cap message list at 200 per channel — trim oldest on append (`MAX_MESSAGES_PER_CHANNEL`)
- Coil image loading: use `crossfade(false)` for message avatars to avoid animation overhead on scroll

## Room / SQLite

- WAL mode enabled: `setJournalMode(RoomDatabase.JournalMode.WRITE_AHEAD_LOGGING)` — concurrent reads/writes
- Use `fallbackToDestructiveMigration()` during active development; add proper migrations before release
- Use `@Upsert` (not `@Insert(onConflict = REPLACE)`) — semantically cleaner, same performance
- DAO writes always async from Store: `appScope.launch { dao.upsert(entity) }` — never block UI
- Cold-start load uses `getLatestByChannel(limit=200)` — NEVER load unbounded lists from DB
- Do not expose `Flow<List<>>` from DAO to UI — expose `StateFlow` from Store instead (hot cache is faster)

## Object allocation

- Avoid creating lambdas in hot paths (scroll handlers, item rendering). Hoist to `remember` or class-level.
- Avoid `String.format()` in tight loops — use `StringBuilder` or pre-format
- Use primitive arrays (`LongArray`) over `List<Long>` for ID collections in hot paths
- Regex cached in `util/ContentParser.kt` as `private val` — never compile Regex inline

## Network

- Proto over JSON: already using protobuf — keep it everywhere, never serialize to JSON for internal use
- Connection reuse: single `OkHttpClient` and `HttpClient` instance (already @Singleton)
- Batch API calls where possible (fetch DM + group in parallel with `async`/`awaitAll`)

## Startup

- On cold start: Room cache loads first → REST fetch runs in background → UI shows cached data immediately
- Defer non-critical initialization: socket connect after first frame renders
- Use `Dispatchers.IO` for DataStore reads on splash
- Profile with Android Studio Profiler: target < 500ms cold start to first content

## Image loading (Coil in Compose)

```kotlin
AsyncImage(
    model = url,
    contentDescription = null,
    modifier = Modifier.size(32.dp).clip(CircleShape),
    contentScale = ContentScale.Crop
)
```

- Set explicit `Modifier.size(...)` for avatars to avoid decoding full-res images
